		)
		(uuid "4a2c39a5-f81b-5d3d-8f29-694fdd60ac7a")
	)
	(text "Every part, pin and net of the Cardputer-Adv, with the values the vendor\ndocuments: connectivity documented from the vendor's public documentation,\nwith Kleidos additions and corrections listed on page 1 (M5Stack's\nCardputer-Adv schematic v1.0 and Stamp-S3 schematic v0.3.3, the docs\npages, the datasheets and bench records each entry cites; README.md and\nnetlist.yaml beside this file). Layout and symbols are this project's.\nNo footprints, no PCB, no part numbers beyond the documented ones.\nValues are as the vendor prints them (10KΩ, 10K/1%, 22uF), but where an\nentry below says otherwise. A value of NC means not fitted: that part\nis marked DNP.\nPages 2 to 5 are the carrier's four sheets, page 6 the module's.\nBoth number their parts from 1, so the module's are numbered +100\nhere (its U1 is U101, its M1, the module's pins, is M101).\nThe module's pins land on the carrier's sockets P1 and P2. A net\nthey share takes the carrier's name (GPIO8 on the module is G8).\nGI and GO are the vendor's names for the Grove pair (GPIO1, GPIO2).\nNets the vendor left unnamed carry names of ours (U2_FB, SD_CS...).\nZones: numbered columns and rows A-H, 50 mm apart, printed in the border."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 103.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.75 1.75)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
